tertiary button is the base for all other buttons in the system. It provides no significant visual treatment other than to provide indication for the user to take a common action."},"172":{"id":"/docs/components/button-23","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#primary","content":"The primary button should be used to indicate the most important action for the user to take in their current experience."},"173":{"id":"/docs/components/button-24","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#secondary","content":"The secondary button indicates an action of secondary importance."},"174":{"id":"/docs/components/button-25","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#tertiary","content":"The tertiary button is the default, low-emphasis style used for common, non-critical actions."},"175":{"id":"/docs/components/button-26","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#critical","content":"The critical button signifies to the user a destructive action will take place."},"176":{"id":"/docs/components/button-27","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#disabled","content":"Any button variant can be disabled to prevent interaction, communicated with reduced opacity and a not-allowed cursor."},"177":{"id":"/docs/components/button-28","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#icon","content":"You may provide an optional `Icon` component to the button. Wrap the text beside an icon in a `Text`. If you do not include text, you must provide an aria-label attribute to identify the purpose of the button. This will produce a square button."},"178":{"id":"/docs/components/button-29","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#icons-and-alignment","content":"Co