x","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#rtl-support","content":"Box uses CSS logical properties (`padding-inline-start`, `padding-block-end`, etc.) which automatically adapt to RTL layouts. No additional configuration is needed."},"2160":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-36","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#design-tokens","content":"All spacing, elevation, and rounding values are derived from the theme. If no theme is provided, default values are used. This ensures consistency across the design system."},"2161":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-37","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#context-and-slots","content":"`BoxContext` supplies default props to Boxes in its subtree. A `slots` map supplies defaults to\nnamed parts; each Box selects one with `slot`. Explicit consumer props override defaults, while\nclasses, styles, and refs are merged. Pass `slot={null}` to opt out of the context."},"2162":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-38","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#context-and-slots","content":"Flex and Grid render through Box and also consume BoxContext. Named slot maps require a matching\nslot unless the provider includes an unslotted default. Nested providers replace the outer context."},"2163":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","type":"page","content":"Flex","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Layout"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/flex"},"2164":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex-0","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/flex","content":"One-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control"},"2165":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/flex-1","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/flex","typ