itle."],[1827,"**ToggleButton Item:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"],[1826,"**ToggleButtonGroup Container:** `data-size`"],[1974,"**Tooltips** use absolute positioning and scroll-aware calculations for accurate placement"],[1963,"**Tooltips**: Show on both hover and focus for keyboard users"],[772,"**Trade-offs:**"],[714,"**Transform**: `rotate`, `flip` for icon transformations"],[528,"**Trigger and calendar**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a calendar icon and the formatted value from the field. `DatePickerCalendar` (and `DateRangePickerCalendar`) is the calendar in the popover it opens: it takes `Calendar` props plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `Calendar` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[1432,"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"],[924,"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"],[2152,"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."],[708,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[1937,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[2219,"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."],[775,"**Use default mode** for SSR applications or when icons appear infrequently"],[776,"**Use sprite mode** when the same icons appear many times (navigation, lists, tables)"],[786,"**Use sprite mode**: For repeated icons, consider sprite mode which consolidates multiple icons into a single SVG sprite sheet, reducing DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[1054,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1436,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1885,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1052,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[1992,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[1929,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[1968,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[1938,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[762,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[1554,"`--color-input-background-default`"],[1551,"`--color-input-background-selected`"],[1560,"`--color-input-text-default`"],[1561,"`--ux-1glcx6s`"],[1549,"`--ux-1m9ys0v`"],[1555,"`--ux-1nu8itt`"],[1558,"`--ux-1sbfig8`"],[1552,"`--ux-sywk25`"],[1564,"`--ux-zvaw3s`"],[206,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[2198,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2200,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2194,"`<Box orientation=\"horizontal\">`"],[2196,"`<Box orientation=\"vertical\">`"],[2201,"`<Flex alignItems=\"center\">`"],[2197,"`<Flex direction=\"column\" >`"],[2195,"`<Flex direction=\"row\" >`"],[2199,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[2148,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[644,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1728,"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."],[1218,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1405,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[445,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[338,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1219,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1406,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[340,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1221,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1843,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1407,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[444,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[339,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1220,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[442,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[441,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[443,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[2140,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[2161,"`BoxContext` supplies default props to Boxes in its subtree. A `slots` map supplies defaults to\nnamed parts; each Box selects one with `slot`. Explicit consumer props override defaults, while\nclasses, styles, and refs are merged. Pass `slot={null}` to opt out of the context."],[490,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[205,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[255,"`CardGroup` uses grid navigation: Tab enters or leaves, arrow keys move between Cards, and Space\nchanges selection. Enter activates row actions or links. Choose selection or `onAction`;\ncombining them prevents pointer selection."],[1949,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[324,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[394,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[412,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[390,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[405,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1772,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[481,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[491,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[492,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[483,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[2106,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1153,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[737,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[740,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[736,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[738,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[739,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[741,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1542,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[530,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[1692,"`Detail` is supporting copy, such as captions and metadata, on the detail ramp. It keeps the\nsurrounding color; add `emphasis=\"passive\"` to mute it."],[564,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[658,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1683,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1691,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[1084,"`Enter/Space`"],[60,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[488,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[606,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[831,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[573,"`Escape`"],[989,"`Escape`"],[1086,"`Escape`"],[1777,"`Escape`"],[643,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[2180,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[745,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[2218,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[660,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[495,"`Icon slot=\"indicator\"` is decorative and receives `aria-hidden=\"true\"` automatically."],[819,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[860,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[2089,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[661,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[2146,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[878,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[2145,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[913,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[203,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[533,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[982,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[977,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1152,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1941,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1611,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1767,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[1027,"`PaginationDots` is decorative and does not replace interactive page\ncontrols."],[839,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[822,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[1078,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[825,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1253,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[1258,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1207,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[2108,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[2109,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[2107,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[991,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[1088,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[577,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[744,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[743,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[440,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1217,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1404,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1216,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1403,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1842,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1841,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[919,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1682,"`size` picks a step on the component's own ramp (`xs` to `2xl`) and changes only the font size."],[1726,"`size` sets every part, each on its own role ramp. Without it, the lockup follows the size\nscope."],[1062,"`size` sets the label, input, and steppers. Without it, the field follows the surrounding size\nscope."],[1893,"`size` sets the label, input, description, and any control composed inside. Without it, the\nfield follows the surrounding size scope."],[545,"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."],[983,"`size` sets the modal's text, controls, and spacing. Without it, the modal follows the size\nscope around its trigger."],[659,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name, and takes the overlay's\ntitle tier, one step above the heading tier."],[2144,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[1460,"`sm`, `md`, or `lg` for the adopted components inside (listed below): their text, controls, and\ndefault spacing."],[95,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1568,"`Space` toggles the switch when it has focus"],[1154,"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."],[93,"`Tab`"],[575,"`Tab`"],[604,"`Tab`"],[833,"`Tab`"],[987,"`Tab`"],[1775,"`Tab`"],[58,"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"],[486,"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"],[1615,"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."],[1612,"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."],[1616,"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."],[1614,"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."],[1119,"`Text slot=\"description\"` is associated automatically, preserving external `aria-describedby` references."],[1680,"`Text` applies the body role and `Detail` the detail role, each at the tier of the nearest\n`SizeProvider`, or `md` outside any scope."],[1679,"`Text` is body copy and `Detail` is supporting copy: captions, metadata, and hints."],[1700,"`TextArea` is the multiline control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` as the parent; see that component for fuller examples."],[1362,"`TextLockup`"],[1732,"`TextLockup` positions and type-sets its parts; you supply them. That means anything else can\nsit alongside them — a call to action, a second paragraph, an image — without the component\ngrowing a prop for it."],[1302,"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."],[958,"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."],[1766,"`TooltipTrigger` wraps a focusable element and a `<Tooltip>`, handling hover/focus state and positioning automatically."],[2100,"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."],[959,"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."],[2110,"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."],[2088,"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."],[1943,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[2093,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[2084,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[2147,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[2086,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[2094,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[2097,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[2143,"`xs` - Extra small spacing"],[1363,"`xs`-`2xl`"],[1944,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[2090,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[2087,"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps t